<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matsudaira Yorishige</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1622–1695</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matsudaira Yorishige was the first lord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takamatsu">Takamatsu</a> domain in Sanuki, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-yorifusa">Tokugawa Yorifusa</a> of Mito and elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-mitsukuni">Tokugawa Mitsukuni</a>. In 1642 he received eastern Sanuki with 120,000 koku, and his line ruled Takamatsu until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a> as close kin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shoguns</a>. He developed the town's water supply and the Ritsurin garden.</p></div>
